WEBVTT

00:30:29.770 --> 00:30:31.210
Sound familiar?

00:30:31.234 --> 00:30:34.076
SK: I knew I was going to come home
about a year later.

00:30:34.100 --> 00:30:35.816
I didn't know exactly when.

00:30:35.840 --> 00:30:42.126
I had to make this mental kind of change
to my whole reference system

00:30:42.150 --> 00:30:44.086
with regards to my life.

00:30:44.110 --> 00:30:46.586
AG: He'd been to space three times before,

00:30:46.610 --> 00:30:50.186
but he'd never been out there for so long
away from everyone he loved.

00:30:50.210 --> 00:30:53.226
SK: And I felt like
I needed to pace myself,

00:30:53.250 --> 00:30:55.656
as you can wind up working too much

00:30:55.680 --> 00:30:58.266
when you go to sleep in your office,

00:30:58.290 --> 00:31:01.288
and you wake up,
and you're still in your office.